  "decision_rule": {
    "primary": "If re-mapping moves pooled PR-AUC by more than the pooled CI on the re-run cells, every T23-T26 conclusion gets a mapping-sensitivity caveat and the cleaned mapping becomes the campaign's recommended default. If not, the 13% literature figure is non-binding here. The agreement table is reported regardless -- the first published error estimate for this mapping pipeline."
  },
  "verdict": "Re-mapping measurably HURTS pooled PR-AUC (relative to the shipped mapping) on [('patient_dropout_rate_yn', 'Phase1')], despite low shipped/remap agreement there (see cell_agreement_table). This is not the direction the plan default framing anticipated: the shipped mapping is not improved upon by this SapBERT nearest-neighbor remap, so it stays the campaign default; the disagreement is reported as an interpretive caveat (condition strings may carry predictive signal beyond what any single ICD code captures), not as grounds to switch mappings. The 13-percent-error-floor literature figure is not vindicated as a quality problem here -- disagreement is real, but cleaning it does not help this benchmark predictions.",
  "git_sha": "f4970dda94d6e122a29d9083b6ebf768ee0f5801-dirty",
  "provenance_note": "git_sha above is dirty (uncommitted working tree at run time). That tree is now committed verbatim at 958ca37 (\"T25/T26/T27 code + P12 disease-holdout splits; SapBERT GPU fix; ignore T25 per-arm run caches\") -- no code changed between this run and that commit. Not re-run for provenance; see docs/open_items_2026-08-28.md A1.",
